taoyao.translation:
The peach tree is young and tender, its blossoms blaze;
this girl is going to her new home, and will bring harmony to her household.
The peach tree is young and tender, its fruit is plump;
this girl is going to her new home, and will bring harmony to her family.
The peach tree is young and tender, its leaves are lush;
this girl is going to her new home, and will bring harmony to the people of her house.

hanguang.translation:
In the south stand tall trees, but one cannot rest beneath them;
on the Han there are roaming girls, but they cannot be won.
The Han is so wide, it cannot be swum;
the Yangtze so long, it cannot be crossed by raft.
Tall rise the tangled brushwood; I will cut the thorn-bush.
When that girl goes to her husband, I would feed her horses.
The Han is so wide, it cannot be swum;
the Yangtze so long, it cannot be crossed by raft.
Tall rise the tangled brushwood; I will cut the artemisia.
When that girl goes to her husband, I would feed her colts.
The Han is so wide, it cannot be swum;
the Yangtze so long, it cannot be crossed by raft.

quechao.translation:
The magpie has a nest, and the dove lives in it;
this girl is going to her new home, and a hundred carriages meet her.
The magpie has a nest, and the dove shares it;
this girl is going to her new home, and a hundred carriages escort her.
The magpie has a nest, and the dove fills it;
this girl is going to her new home, and a hundred carriages complete the rite.

yanyan.translation:
The swallows fly, their wings uneven;
she is going home, and I see her far into the fields;
I gaze after her, cannot see her, and my tears fall like rain.
The swallows fly, now rising, now dipping;
she is going home, and I escort her far;
I gaze after her, cannot see her, and stand a long while weeping.
The swallows fly, their calls going down and up;
she is going home, and I see her far to the south;
I gaze after her, cannot see her, and it truly wears my heart.
My second sister is trustworthy,
her heart honest and deep;
ever gentle and kind,
good and careful in herself.
She remembers our late lord,
to encourage me, the one who rules.

kaifeng.translation:
The warm wind comes from the south and blows on the jujube shoots;
the shoots are soft and tender; Mother has toiled hard.
The warm wind comes from the south and blows on the jujube branches fit for firewood;
Mother is wise and good, and none of us is a worthy man.
There is a cold spring below Jun;
she has seven sons, and Mother has suffered hardship.
The yellow birds sing sweetly, their notes so fair;
she has seven sons, and none comforts Mother's heart.

younvtongche.translation:
A girl shares my carriage, her face like hibiscus flowers;
she moves as if on wings, wearing fine jade pendants.
That fair Meng Jiang is truly lovely and graceful.
A girl walks with me, her face like hibiscus blossom;
she moves as if on wings, her jade pendants chiming.
That fair Meng Jiang - her good name is never forgotten.

wanqiu.translation:
How you sway and dance, up on Wanqiu,
truly I love, but have no hope.
Kan-kan beats the drum at the foot of Wanqiu;
winter or summer, you hold your egret feathers.
Kan-kan beats the pottery drum on the road of Wanqiu;
winter or summer, you hold your egret-feather fan.

beishan.translation:
I climb that northern hill and pick wolfberries.
Strong young gentlemen work from morning till night.
The king's work never ends, and my parents worry.
Under the broad sky, none is not the king's land;
to the ends of the earth, none is not the king's servant.
The officials are unfair; I alone am worked hard.
The four stallions press on; the king's work is unending.
They praise me for not being old, and for being in my prime.
My strength is firm; I manage the four quarters.
Some rest at ease at home, some wear themselves out for the state;
some lie down in bed, some never stop travelling;
some do not know the cry of toil, some are wretched with labour;
some idle about, lying back, some are swamped with the king's affairs;
some drink and make merry, some are anxious for fear of blame;
some come and go and talk idly of policy, some leave no task undone.
